---
import ProjectShell from './ProjectShell.astro';
import '../styles/nokia-analytics-case-study.scss';
import '../styles/page-view.scss';
---

<ProjectShell title="Telecom Analytics & Cost Optimization" previous={{title:'Ayu Sales Intelligence & Field Force Optimization',href:'/projects/ayu-sales-intelligence'}} next={{title:'Integrated Channels Suite',href:'/projects/integrated-channels'}}>
  <main class="case-study nokia-case">
    <section class="case-page nokia-overview" id="overview"><div class="case-page-inner">
      <div class="case-kicker"><i></i>01 / OVERVIEW <span>NOKIA NETWORKS · TELECOM ANALYTICS</span></div>
      <div class="nokia-intro"><div><h1>Connect where the network is with what it costs.</h1><p class="case-lede">An enterprise analytics product for infrastructure capital efficiency: combine rollout, field, finance and geographic context so engineering and leadership can see asset visibility gaps and act.</p><div class="analytics-thesis"><b>ASSET IDENTITY</b><i>+</i><b>GEOGRAPHY</b><i>+</i><b>COST CONTEXT</b><i>→</i><strong>BETTER INVESTMENT DECISIONS</strong></div></div><aside class="nokia-map-card"><div class="map-label">NETWORK VISIBILITY MODEL</div><svg viewBox="0 0 440 290" role="img" aria-label="Conceptual network asset map with linked sites"><path class="land-shape" d="M34 75 95 35 160 58 212 31 280 63 379 45 414 110 370 158 398 222 323 259 255 231 199 262 142 225 83 245 48 185Z"/><path class="map-link" d="M92 90 193 112 297 77 354 156 255 204 150 179 92 90M193 112 255 204M297 77 255 204M150 179 354 156"/><g class="map-site"><circle cx="92" cy="90" r="8"/><circle cx="193" cy="112" r="8"/><circle cx="297" cy="77" r="8"/><circle cx="354" cy="156" r="8"/><circle cx="255" cy="204" r="8"/><circle cx="150" cy="179" r="8"/></g></svg><div class="map-legend"><span>Asset</span><span>Network link</span><span>Regional view</span></div></aside></div>
      <div class="nokia-result"><strong>15%–20%</strong><span>CapEx / OpEx savings via asset visibility optimisation</span><small>SUPPLIED PROJECT RESULT</small></div>
      <div class="case-page-foot"><span>01</span><i></i><b>ENTERPRISE DATA · SPATIAL VISIBILITY · COST INTELLIGENCE</b></div>
    </div></section>

    <section class="case-page nokia-ecosystem" id="ecosystem"><div class="case-page-inner">
      <header class="case-heading"><div class="case-kicker"><i></i>02 / ECOSYSTEM</div><h2>Join network activity, finance and place.</h2><p>Source domains converge into an analytics layer; different operators use the same picture to make distinct decisions.</p></header>
      <div class="nokia-ecosystem-map"><div class="source-column"><b>NETWORK SOURCES</b><article>Hardware rollouts<span>Deployment status · asset register</span></article><article>Field operations<span>Site updates · work records</span></article><article>Network telemetry<span>Performance · utilisation context</span></article><article>Finance data<span>CapEx · OpEx · cost centre</span></article><article>Geographic data<span>Coordinates · region · site boundary</span></article></div><div class="source-converge"><svg viewBox="0 0 250 400" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M0 40C120 40 80 200 245 200M0 120C120 120 80 200 245 200M0 200H245M0 280C120 280 80 200 245 200M0 360C120 360 80 200 245 200"/><circle cx="236" cy="200" r="7"/></svg></div><div class="analytics-core"><small>DATA / ANALYTICS PLATFORM</small><b>Asset identity<br/>+ spatial model<br/>+ cost measures</b><span>Trusted joins · KPI definitions · freshness</span></div><div class="decision-fan"><svg viewBox="0 0 220 400" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M0 200C100 200 90 45 215 45M0 200H215M0 200C100 200 90 355 215 355"/></svg></div><div class="decision-column"><b>DECISION USERS</b><article>Engineering<span>Rollout · utilisation · site priorities</span></article><article>Field operations<span>Asset verification · local follow-up</span></article><article>Finance leadership<span>Investment · regional cost · efficiency</span></article></div></div>
      <div class="case-page-foot"><span>02</span><i></i><b>SOURCES → SHARED MODEL → ROLE-BASED DECISIONS</b></div>
    </div></section>

    <section class="case-page nokia-challenge" id="challenge"><div class="case-page-inner">
      <header class="case-heading"><div class="case-kicker"><i></i>03 / CHALLENGE</div><h2>The asset existed; the decision context did not.</h2><p>Siloed field-operation databases disconnected infrastructure location from rollout status and financial visibility.</p></header>
      <div class="silo-story"><div class="silo-before"><small>BEFORE · ISOLATED VIEWS</small><div class="silo-databases"><article><b>Field files</b><span>Local asset records</span></article><article><b>Rollout data</b><span>Deployment milestones</span></article><article><b>Finance extracts</b><span>Cost by period</span></article><article><b>Map layers</b><span>Geography without context</span></article></div><div class="silo-gap">NO STABLE ASSET JOIN · NO SHARED LOCATION + COST VIEW</div></div><div class="visibility-consequence"><div><small>WHAT STAYS HIDDEN</small><strong>Overlap</strong><strong>Unmapped assets</strong><strong>Underused capacity</strong><strong>Rollout inefficiency</strong></div><div class="cost-blindspot"><b>Multi-million-dollar inefficiencies</b><span>described in the project context become harder to identify, explain and route to an owner.</span></div></div><div class="silo-after"><small>AFTER · DECISION-READY CONTEXT</small><div><b>ASSET</b><i>+</i><b>LOCATION</b><i>+</i><b>ROLLOUT</b><i>+</i><b>COST</b><i>→</i><strong>INVESTIGATE</strong></div></div></div>
      <div class="case-page-foot"><span>03</span><i></i><b>DATA SILOS · SPATIAL BLIND SPOTS · COST EXPOSURE</b></div>
    </div></section>

    <section class="case-page nokia-strategy" id="strategy"><div class="case-page-inner">
      <header class="case-heading"><div class="case-kicker"><i></i>04 / STRATEGY</div><h2>Trust the join before trusting the insight.</h2><p>Build a reliable asset spine, pair geography with cost and let users drill from portfolio signal to regional evidence.</p></header>
      <div class="analytics-strategy"><div class="strategy-matrix"><div class="matrix-label y-label">DECISION CONFIDENCE ↑</div><div class="matrix-label x-label">SOURCE / SPATIAL COMPLETENESS →</div><article class="matrix-1"><b>01 · IDENTITY</b><strong>Standardise asset keys</strong><span>Resolve source references to one asset view.</span></article><article class="matrix-2"><b>02 · JOIN</b><strong>Attach geography + cost</strong><span>Expose location, rollout and financial context.</span></article><article class="matrix-3"><b>03 · MEASURE</b><strong>Define decision KPIs</strong><span>Connect metric meaning to stakeholder action.</span></article><article class="matrix-4"><b>04 · DRILL</b><strong>Portfolio → region → site</strong><span>Trace executive signal to local evidence.</span></article></div><aside class="decision-ladder"><small>ANALYTICS PRODUCT PRINCIPLE</small><b>Executive signal</b><i>↓</i><b>Regional comparison</b><i>↓</i><b>Asset / site evidence</b><i>↓</i><b>Engineering or finance action</b></aside></div>
      <div class="case-page-foot"><span>04</span><i></i><b>IDENTITY · GEO JOIN · KPI · DRILL-DOWN</b></div>
    </div></section>

    <section class="case-page nokia-scope" id="pm-scope"><div class="case-page-inner">
      <header class="case-heading"><div class="case-kicker"><i></i>05 / PM SCOPE</div><h2>Define the semantic layer users can make decisions with.</h2><p>Product management tied data definitions, analytical questions and dashboard hierarchy to engineering and finance workflows.</p></header>
      <div class="semantic-board"><div class="semantic-rail"><article><small>DISCOVER</small><b>Source inventory</b><span>Owner · refresh · field meaning</span></article><i>→</i><article><small>DEFINE</small><b>Asset dimensions</b><span>Identity · geography · lifecycle</span></article><i>→</i><article><small>MODEL</small><b>Cost + rollout KPIs</b><span>Measure definition · grain · filters</span></article><i>→</i><article><small>DELIVER</small><b>Analytics views</b><span>SQL needs · Power BI / Tableau</span></article></div><div class="semantic-contract"><b>DATA CONTRACT</b><span>What does this asset mean?</span><span>How fresh is this view?</span><span>Which source owns the field?</span><span>What decision should this KPI change?</span><span>How can an engineer or finance lead verify it?</span></div><div class="stakeholder-bar"><b>ENGINEERING</b><i>↔</i><b>FIELD OPERATIONS</b><i>↔</i><b>FINANCE</b><i>↔</i><b>ANALYTICS / DATA</b></div></div>
      <div class="case-page-foot"><span>05</span><i></i><b>SOURCE DEFINITION · KPI SEMANTICS · DASHBOARD STRATEGY</b></div>
    </div></section>

    <section class="case-page nokia-architecture" id="architecture"><div class="case-page-inner">
      <header class="case-heading"><div class="case-kicker"><i></i>06 / ARCHITECTURE</div><h2>Converge independent domains through an asset-centred model.</h2><p>Conceptual data architecture: quality and identity bind the feeds before spatial and financial analysis.</p></header>
      <div class="data-architecture"><div class="domain-sources"><article><b>OPERATIONS</b><span>Rollout · field records</span></article><article><b>TELEMETRY</b><span>Network · utilisation</span></article><article><b>FINANCE</b><span>CapEx · OpEx · cost centre</span></article><article><b>GEOGRAPHY</b><span>Site · region · coordinates</span></article></div><div class="ingestion-layer"><svg viewBox="0 0 1000 90" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M125 0V70H875V0M375 0V70M625 0V70M875 0V70M500 70V90"/></svg><b>INGEST · VALIDATE · FRESHNESS CHECK</b></div><div class="asset-model"><div class="data-dim"><small>CONFORMED MODEL</small><strong>Asset identity</strong><span>Stable key · lineage · ownership</span></div><div class="data-dim geo-dim"><small>SPATIAL JOIN</small><strong>Location + region</strong><span>Coordinate quality · geographic grain</span></div><div class="data-dim cost-dim"><small>MEASURE LAYER</small><strong>Cost + rollout</strong><span>CapEx / OpEx · period · status</span></div></div><div class="consumer-layer"><article><b>ANALYTICS</b><span>Trend · variance · comparison</span></article><article><b>SPATIAL INTELLIGENCE</b><span>Asset map · overlap · visibility</span></article><article><b>DECISION VIEWS</b><span>Executive · regional · site drill-down</span></article></div><div class="architecture-quality"><span>Source coverage</span><span>Asset match rate</span><span>Refresh timestamp</span><span>Quality exceptions</span></div></div>
      <div class="case-page-foot"><span>06</span><i></i><b>MULTI-SOURCE DATA FABRIC · ASSET-CENTRED ANALYTICS</b></div>
    </div></section>

    <section class="case-page nokia-delivery" id="delivery"><div class="case-page-inner">
      <header class="case-heading"><div class="case-kicker"><i></i>07 / DELIVERY</div><h2>Roll out insight at the level teams act.</h2><p>Layer enterprise views from local validation through regional comparison to leadership visibility.</p></header>
      <div class="regional-rollout"><div class="rollout-layers"><article class="layer-local"><small>LOCAL / SITE</small><strong>Validate asset and geography</strong><span>Field and engineering confirm identity, location and status.</span><b>TRUST THE RECORD</b></article><div class="rollout-up">↑ ALIGN MEANING + FEEDBACK ↑</div><article class="layer-region"><small>REGIONAL</small><strong>Compare deployment and cost</strong><span>Engineering leads examine variance, overlap and utilisation context.</span><b>PRIORITISE FOLLOW-UP</b></article><div class="rollout-up">↑ STANDARDISE KPI + OWNERSHIP ↑</div><article class="layer-enterprise"><small>ENTERPRISE</small><strong>See capital efficiency trends</strong><span>Finance leadership compares investment with mapped infrastructure.</span><b>DIRECT DECISIONS</b></article></div><aside class="rollout-conditions"><b>EXPANSION CONDITIONS</b><span>Source reconciliation</span><span>Spatial validation</span><span>KPI agreement</span><span>Regional ownership</span><span>Feedback incorporated</span></aside></div>
      <div class="case-page-foot"><span>07</span><i></i><b>LOCAL VALIDATION → REGIONAL USE → ENTERPRISE VIEW</b></div>
    </div></section>

    <section class="case-page nokia-explorer" id="product-explorer"><div class="case-page-inner">
      <header class="case-heading"><div class="case-kicker"><i></i>08 / PRODUCT EXPLORER</div><h2>A spatial cost-intelligence command centre.</h2><p>Enterprise analyst view · connect CapEx / OpEx, regional variance and mapped infrastructure in one decision surface.</p></header>
      <div class="analytics-command"><div class="command-top"><div><small>NETWORK CAPITAL EFFICIENCY</small><b>Infrastructure portfolio</b></div><div class="command-filters"><span>Region ▾</span><span>Period ▾</span><span>Asset class ▾</span></div></div><div class="executive-strip"><article><small>CapEx</small><b>Portfolio trend</b><i class="trend capex"></i><span>Drill to deployment</span></article><article><small>OpEx</small><b>Cost variance</b><i class="trend opex"></i><span>Compare by region</span></article><article><small>Asset visibility</small><b>Mapped / unmapped</b><div class="visibility-dots"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></div><span>Coverage signal</span></article><article><small>Rollout</small><b>Status by region</b><div class="rollout-bars"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></div><span>Plan · deploy · verify</span></article></div><div class="command-body"><div class="spatial-panel"><div class="panel-top"><b>GEOGRAPHIC ASSET VIEW</b><span>Infrastructure layer · rollout status</span></div><svg viewBox="0 0 540 270" role="img" aria-label="Illustrative geographic view of connected network infrastructure assets"><path class="geo-outline" d="M34 68 101 32 168 49 224 25 291 54 358 37 441 68 501 118 464 166 483 220 405 241 347 213 280 246 212 215 143 239 83 203 45 143Z"/><path class="geo-edges" d="M83 100 170 91 246 118 335 82 410 126 444 184 337 191 272 160 193 178 119 151 83 100M170 91 193 178M246 118 272 160M335 82 337 191M410 126 337 191"/><g class="geo-assets"><circle cx="83" cy="100" r="7"/><circle cx="170" cy="91" r="7"/><circle cx="246" cy="118" r="7"/><circle cx="335" cy="82" r="7"/><circle cx="410" cy="126" r="7"/><circle cx="444" cy="184" r="7"/><circle cx="337" cy="191" r="7"/><circle cx="193" cy="178" r="7"/></g></svg><div class="spatial-legend"><span>Active asset</span><span>Rollout link</span><span>Needs verification</span></div></div><aside class="cost-driver-panel"><div class="panel-top"><b>COST DRIVERS</b><span>Regional drill-down</span></div><article><span>Deployment variance</span><i><b style="--w:72%"></b></i></article><article><span>Unmapped infrastructure</span><i><b style="--w:48%"></b></i></article><article><span>Utilisation context</span><i><b style="--w:65%"></b></i></article><article><span>Duplicate visibility check</span><i><b style="--w:36%"></b></i></article><div class="driver-note">Illustrative analytical categories · confirm source coverage and drill into asset evidence before action.</div></aside></div><div class="command-footer"><span>SELECTED ASSET</span><b>Site → rollout record → geography → cost centre → engineering owner</b><span>FRESHNESS: SOURCE TIMESTAMP REQUIRED</span></div></div>
      <div class="case-page-foot"><span>08</span><i></i><b>MAP · COST DRIVERS · ROLLOUT · ASSET DRILL-DOWN</b></div>
    </div></section>

    <section class="case-page nokia-impact" id="impact"><div class="case-page-inner">
      <header class="case-heading"><div class="case-kicker"><i></i>09 / IMPACT</div><h2>Asset visibility turns disconnected records into cost action.</h2><p>The supplied savings range is linked to the product mechanism that enables investigation and optimisation.</p></header>
      <div class="cost-impact"><div class="savings-card"><small>SUPPLIED PROJECT RESULT</small><strong>15%–20%</strong><span>CapEx / OpEx savings via asset visibility optimisation</span></div><div class="impact-chain"><article><b>01 · INTEGRATE</b><strong>Join operational + finance data</strong><span>Shared asset identity and source lineage.</span></article><i>→</i><article><b>02 · LOCATE</b><strong>Map infrastructure</strong><span>Expose spatial overlap and visibility gaps.</span></article><i>→</i><article><b>03 · UNDERSTAND</b><strong>Explain cost drivers</strong><span>Drill through region, rollout and asset context.</span></article><i>→</i><article><b>04 · OPTIMISE</b><strong>Change investment decision</strong><span>Engineering and finance act on verified evidence.</span></article></div><div class="impact-integrity">Outcome range is project-provided; do not convert it to a single-point estimate without confirming scope and measurement basis.</div></div>
      <div class="case-page-foot"><span>09</span><i></i><b>INTEGRATION → VISIBILITY → SPATIAL INSIGHT → COST ACTION</b></div>
    </div></section>

    <section class="case-page nokia-leadership" id="leadership"><div class="case-page-inner">
      <header class="case-heading"><div class="case-kicker"><i></i>10 / PRODUCT LEADERSHIP</div><h2>Analytics trust depends on what users cannot see.</h2><p>Freshness, coverage, spatial accuracy and governance determine whether a dashboard can support a capital decision.</p></header>
      <div class="trust-model"><div class="trust-pyramid"><article class="trust-top"><b>DECISION TRUST</b><span>Can I act on this view?</span></article><article class="trust-mid"><b>SPATIAL ACCURACY</b><span>Does the asset map to the right place?</span></article><article class="trust-low"><b>DATA QUALITY + FRESHNESS</b><span>Is the source complete, current and owned?</span></article><article class="trust-base"><b>SOURCE COVERAGE + GOVERNANCE</b><span>Can the lineage and definition be verified?</span></article></div><div class="maturity-roadmap"><small>ANALYTICS MATURITY PATH</small><article><b>NOW</b><strong>Trusted periodic reporting</strong><span>Stable asset joins · refresh labels · quality exceptions</span></article><article><b>NEXT</b><strong>Near-real-time visibility</strong><span>Fresher telemetry with operational freshness controls</span></article><article><b>FUTURE</b><strong>Predictive planning</strong><span>Forecast rollout and cost opportunity when data maturity supports it</span></article></div></div>
      <div class="case-page-foot"><span>10</span><i></i><b>LATENCY · QUALITY · SPATIAL PRECISION · GOVERNANCE</b></div>
    </div></section>
  </main>
</ProjectShell>
